{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361989-which-historical-eras","id":1361989,"title":"Which Historical Eras?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-01-19T14:40:59-08:00","id":1361989,"title":"Which Historical Eras?","content":"We're clearly getting Adventure! first. (Let the heavens be praised!!!!!) But what other historical Eras do we want? <br /> <br /> In my case I'd want...<br /> <br /> 1) 17th through 18th century Asia. Clearly to vast a subject, I'd expect a core book on Qing China and then branching out to Japan, India, Indonesia, et al. Wuxia fighting rules would support Adventure! and the Core setting.<br /> <br /> 2) Age of Sail, the Elizabethan Sea Dogs, the Sea Beggers, the early transoceanic navigation, and PIRATES!!! Lots of swashbuckling, conspiracy, Hermetic Occultists who touched the flux and thing it's the Azoth! Witch-hunts, colonial rebellion, the 15' , the '45, and more.<br /> <br /> 3) The Classical world.<br /> <br /> 4) The Arabian Nights.<br /> <br /> 5) The Age of Heroes. Everything from the Tain, to the Homeric epics, to the Mahabharata, and points east!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T15:07:55-08:00","id":1362000,"title":"","content":"I'm guessing after Assassins will probably be \u00c6gis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T18:04:38-08:00","id":1362029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361989-which-historical-eras?p=1362000#post1362000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm guessing after Assassins will probably be \u00c6gis.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fingers crossed!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3631-adamrice","name":"AdamRice","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"18"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-19T18:31:23-08:00","id":1362034,"title":"","content":"The impression I have is that the plan is \u00c6on, Aberrant, Adventure, Assassins, and then maybe \u00c6gis or some other setting. I suspect we will get some sort of announcement of future plans in the later third of the year, if we are fortunate.<br /> <br /> I think samurai era Japan would be an interesting historical setting for core talents (or Assassins).<br /> Also 1960s James Bond/Modesty Blase style spy adventures would be pretty cool.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T02:43:46-08:00","id":1362077,"title":"","content":"The Renaissance! I read Marvels Jonathan Hickman Shield series and I love the idea that Da Vinci is a handsome you literally Reed Richards level genius!<br /> <br /> In my Apeiron: Trinity setting one of Hammersmith\u2019s secret research artifacts was the secret notes of Da Vinci. And unknown to everyone Da Vinci May be the result of why that world split into three parallel universes after The Hammersmith event. Da Vinci retreated to make his eternal city in a pocket dimension. Three Da Vinci\u2019s to be exact from parallel worlds that were exactly the same until the Hammersmith incident.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T06:10:42-08:00","