"avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T11:10:06-08:00","id":1362170,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jetstream</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361989-which-historical-eras?p=1362137#post1362137\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Given that Ian talks about it a lot, I\u2019m guessing that Anima is next on the docket.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yes, I'd forgotten about that one. So, yeah, probably Aberrant, Adventure, Assassins, Anima, \u00c6gis, and then something new, maybe.<br /> <br /> My ultimate unlikely to ever happen wish setting would be an official Venture Brothers setting book.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T12:39:24-08:00","id":1362196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>johntfs</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361989-which-historical-eras?p=1362090#post1362090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1601-dreaminggod\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1601_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1601\" data-vbnamecard=\"1601\">Dreaminggod</a> is already doing something like this, but how about Trinity: Antediluvian? Basically a full-on Atlantis/Ancient Alien mish-mash of advance prehistorical civilizations including Novas, Psiads and Talents.<br /> <br /> Also maybe pre-colonial First Nations of North and South America.</div> </div> </div> </div> Both cool and the second out of the box. Once some of the others are up (particularly Age of Sail) then the Pre-contact Americas become an interesting stand alone easily sold as an adjunct to other settings. Once you can sell it then it can prove it's stand alone potential.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T12:40:47-08:00","id":1362198,"title":"","content":"I'm still hoping for a greater time war setting, but historicals give a Time War developed venues.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T15:18:47-08:00","id":1362250,"title":"","content":"Just off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> 1980s action heroes<br /> 1970s Adventure as mentioned in the original first ed timelines<br /> 1960s secret agents<br /> 1950s atomic science fiction/Adventure<br /> 1940s WW2 action<br /> <br /> Victorian Era Adventure<br /> Wild West<br /> <br /> American Revolution/Napoleonic Wars<br /> <br /> Europe in the late 16th century<br /> <br /> The Japanese Sengoku/Warring States Period <br /> <br /> The Chinese Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms Period<br /> <br /> Europe in 800 AD, with Charlemagne's Holy Roman Empire, the Byzantines, the Vikings, and various other interesting forces<br /> <br /> Rome during the Five Good Emperors Period<br /> <br /> This just being regular historical settings for the Core Talents or Adventure's expanded set up, as opposed to radical divergences.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>What is tolerance? It is the consequence of humanity. We are all formed of frailty and error; let us pardon reciprocally each other's folly. That is the first law of nature.</i><br /> Voltaire, &quot;Tolerance&quot; (1764)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12890-no-one-of-consequence","name":"No One of Consequence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12890_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-20T19:17:02-08:00","id":1362318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361989-which-historical-eras?p=1362034#post1362034\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The impression I have is that the plan is \u00c6on, Aberrant, Adventure, Assassins, and then maybe \u00c6gis or some other setting. I suspect we will get some sort of announcement of future plans in the later third of the year, if we are fortunate.<br /> <br /> I think samurai era Japan would be an interesting historical setting for core talents (or Assassins).<br /> Also 1960s James Bond/Modesty Blase style spy adventures would be pretty cool.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I feel like I was one of 9 people who really, really enjoyed The Man From UNCLE film. Cold War era spy stuff is a personal favorite. I really tried to like SpyCraft - and they worked their asses off on the game - but I think that Talents could populate such fantastic setting under the OP/StoryPath rules. Secret societies, terrorism, alphabet agencies run amok, conspiracies, nuclear brinksmanship, Operation Paperclip, MK Ultra, the space race and a car or two that can go underwater. <br /> <br /> I'm also a dork for samurai - SIGN ME UP FOR YOUR NEWSLETTER, No One Of Consequence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7165-queen-anne-country","name":"Queen Anne Country","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T06:03:29-08:00","id":1362384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>No One of Consequence</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1361989-which-historical-eras?p=1362170#post1362170\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ah, yes, I'd forgotten about that one. So, yeah, probably Aberrant, Adventure, Assassins, Anima, \u00c6gis, and then something new, maybe.<br /> <br /> My ultimate unlikely to ever happen wish setting would be an official Venture Brothers setting book.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Venture brothers has influenced me more then you can imagine! Specially the origins of the League and the Orb. It\u2019s up their with the League of Extrodinary Gentleman and the Shield Miniseries!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-01-21T07:40:42-08:00","id":1362405,"title":"","content":"We need to have the Guild of Calamitous Intent in Assassin.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2318-johntfs","name":"johntfs","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;